      "message": "1. Instead of defining a separate `MIXED_PRECISION_SOLVER_CONFIGS` that only tests `EIGEN` and `EIGEN_SPARSE`, please use the existing `DENSE_SOLVER_CONFIGS` (`EIGEN`, `LAPACK`, `CUDA`) and `SPARSE_SOLVER_CONFIGS` (`SUITE_SPARSE`, `EIGEN_SPARSE`, `ACCELERATE_SPARSE`, `CUDA_SPARSE`), since all of them support `use_mixed_precision_solves \u003d true`. (For `SUITE_SPARSE` with mixed precision, guard with `#ifndef CERES_NO_CHOLMOD_FLOAT`.)\n\n2. We do not need to test both `0` and `2` refinement iterations (`MIXED_PRECISION_REFINEMENT_LIMITS \u003d [0, 2]`). Testing with `use_mixed_precision_solves \u003d true` and `max_num_refinement_iterations \u003d 2` (with suffix `_MixedPrecision` / `_mixed_test.cc`) already exercises both the single-precision factorization and iterative refinement without doubling the number of generated test binaries.",
      "revId": "94faf5e723f9a9caf60e5dad3f0ca5781691e196",
      "serverId": "cdcfcfbe-2044-3b1f-b5d4-da77ad542329"
